{"user": "What should i have done differently", "user_ts": "2026-08-18T11:52:25.747188+00:00", "assistant": "From the final board, the big issue was **corners and stable edges**.\n\nWhat to do differently next time:\n\n- **Fight for corners / don\u2019t give them away.** White ended with **a1, h1, and a8**, while Black only had **h8**. Corners can\u2019t be flipped, so White\u2019s edges became very stable.\n- **Be careful with squares next to empty corners** \u2014 like **b1, a2, b2** near a1, or **g1/g2/h2** near h1. Those often let White take the corner.\n- **Don\u2019t chase the biggest immediate flip.** In endgames, a move that flips 5 now may let White take a corner and flip 10 later.\n- **Think mobility:** choose moves that leave White with few legal replies, or force White into bad corner-adjacent moves.\n\nSimple rule: before each move ask, **\u201cDoes this give White a corner or an easy edge next turn?\u201d**", "assistant_started_ts": "2026-08-18T11:52:31.794993+00:00", "assistant_ts": "2026-08-18T11:52:34.786500+00:00", "annotation_user": {"final": ["Solution Request"], "consensus": ["Solution Request"], "votes": {"Solution Request": 3}, "confidence": {"Solution Request": 1.0}, "per_model": {"llama": ["Solution Request"], "sonnet": ["Solution Request"], "gpt": ["Solution Request"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "arbiter_used": false}, "annotation_assistant_fine": {"final": ["Board Report", "Local Justification", "General Principle"], "consensus": ["Board Report", "Local Justification", "General Principle"], "votes": {"Board Report": 3, "Local Justification": 3, "General Principle": 3}, "confidence": {"Board Report": 1.0, "Local Justification": 1.0, "General Principle": 1.0}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["Board Report", "Local Justification", "General Principle"], "llama": ["Board Report", "Local Justification", "General Principle"], "sonnet": ["Board Report", "Local Justification", "General Principle"]}, "n_valid":